# Optional overrides for `.devcontainer/docker-compose.yml` (Compose interpolation).
# Copy to `.devcontainer/.env` and edit. The file is gitignored.
#
# Compose loads this file when the **project directory** is `.devcontainer/`
# (`docker compose --project-directory .devcontainer …`) or when you open the
# Dev Container in the IDE (same project directory). If you run plain
# `docker compose -f .devcontainer/docker-compose.yml` from the repo root **without**
# `--project-directory`, Compose may not pick up this file — use `./scripts/devcontainer-run.sh`
# instead (it pins the project directory and auto-sets rootless uid mapping).
#
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Rootful Docker (Docker Desktop, classic root daemon, CI):
#   Leave both unset. The container runs as the built-in `node` user
#   (uid=1000, gid=1000), which matches typical Linux host users with uid 1000.
#
# Rootful Linux with host uid **not** 1000 (e.g. second desktop user):
#   You may see the same EACCES as rootless. Try matching the host (advanced):
#     DEV_UID=<output of id -u>
#     DEV_GID=<output of id -g>
#   If tools complain about HOME, run CLI commands via the wrapper scripts and keep
#   working in `/workspace` only, or ask the maintainer docs for your distro.
#
# Rootless Docker (`docker info` contains `rootless: true`):
#   The default `node` user cannot write the bind-mounted repo. Either:
#   - Use `./scripts/devcontainer-run.sh …` (sets DEV_UID/DEV_GID automatically), or
#   - Export / configure:
#
#     DEV_UID=0
#     DEV_GID=0
#
#   Files written from inside the container will be owned by your host user
#   on disk (not by real host root). For **Reopen in Container** / Cursor Dev
#   Containers, create `.devcontainer/.env` with those lines — the IDE does not
#   run the shell wrapper.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
#
# Future / local-only (not wired into Compose yet; placeholders for experiments):
#   # GUARDSLEEP_SIGNALING_LAN_IP=192.168.1.10
#
# If `./scripts/devcontainer-run.sh` still runs as uid 1000 and hits permission errors,
# either uncomment DEV_UID/DEV_GID below or set on the host for one command only:
#   GUARDSLEEP_DEVCONTAINER_UID=0 GUARDSLEEP_DEVCONTAINER_GID=0 ./scripts/devcontainer-run.sh …
# (See docs/contributing/development.md — only safe on rootless / mapped setups.)

# DEV_UID=0
# DEV_GID=0
